Contract proof:

- `AppRiskDetectionCandidateSchema` requires schema version, platform,
  risk signal, source kind, candidate state, publisher trust state,
  confidence, evidence refs, source refs, policy candidate action,
  risk app policy target kind, ask parent routing, no-direct-enforcement,
  no-content claim, and parent-surface disclosure.
- `AppRiskDetectionMatrixSchema` requires nonempty unique candidates.
- Rules reject missing evidence, mismatched source/state pairs, local AI rows
  without digest refs, parent overrides that mutate raw identity, unknown
  publisher rows above review confidence, and rows that try to become direct
  enforcement.
- `AppRiskDetectionMatrix` includes known VPN/proxy, remote desktop,
  torrent/download, AI chatbot, unknown name, unknown publisher/hash, local AI
  digest, and parent display override rows.
- `packages/parent-domain/tests/app-riskdetection.test.ts` proves the contract
  against real Effect Schema parsers and existing policy-target compiler rules.
